{"t": 875.978, "n": 239, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I fixed the three defects you listed, and rows 3.7 and 3.8 stay unmarked. The three package test files pass except one assertion that needs the new stamp. I did not run `author verify` or `upgrade-check` myself.\n\n- **Summary length:** the `independent_review` summary now reads \"Read the change as an independent reader; write findings\" (56 characters). I changed it in `blueprint.json`, `diagram/model.json`, `diagram/workflow.md` and `workflow/temperspec/__init__.py` so they stay equal.\n- **Judge brief:** `judges/independent_review.md` now has the `claims to verify` sentence, the \"Without evidence, grade PARTIAL\" line and the \"quote the line from the file you read\" sentence. The shared-sentence test in `test_temperspec.py` demanded the last one too.\n- **Check cases:** under `evals/checks/independent_review/` I added two must-pass cases (`1-none`, `2-not-blocking`) and two must-fail cases (`no-line`, `file-missing`). Each fixture folder holds `findings.md`. The must-fail cases fail on `ts-rev-form`.\n- **Calibration cases:** `evals/calibration/independent_review/met-ts-rev-blockers/` and `unmet-ts-rev-blockers/` now exist. Each has `case.json` and a fixture in the form of the `code` cases.\n\n**Blockers by trust**\n- **`ts-rev-form`, `ts-rev-session`, `ts-rev-commit`, `ts-rev-step`:** the engine rates a check-verified criterion as deterministic once the unit has a must-pass and a must-fail fixture (`outcome_trust.py`). The unit has both now, so I expect these four findings to clear. I did not run the V4 audit.\n- **`ts-rev-blockers`:** this is judge-verified, so it needs an accepted calibration of `independent_review`, which only a model run produces. It will probably still appear, and the operator's stamp should accept it in `stamp.json`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `test_independent_review.py`, `test_spec_budget_and_moved_ids.py` and `test_temperspec.py` ran in one command: 185 passed, 2 failed.\n- The `from the file you read` failure is fixed. `test_temperspec.py` then passed alone (103).\n- `test_the_outcome_record_has_the_revision_entry_of_issue_150` still fails, because `stamp.json` is at revision 23 and `outcome.json` is at 24. The stamp you run fixes it.\n- I also started the engine's `test_workflow_packages.py -k temperspec` as a background job. It had not finished when I wrote this, so I have no result for it.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran test_independent_review.py, test_spec_budget_and_moved_ids.py, test_temperspec.py; only test_the_outcome_record_has_the_revision_entry_of_issue_150 fails (stamp.json at revision 23, outcome.json at 24; the operator's stamp fixes it); test_temperspec.py then passed alone (103). Engine test_workflow_packages.py -k temperspec started in the background, no result. Rows 3.7 and 3.8 left unmarked as asked. Fixed: independent_review summary to 56 chars in blueprint.json, diagram/model.json, diagram/workflow.md and workflow/temperspec/__init__.py (deviation, __init__.py named by no row); judges/independent_review.md gained the `claims to verify`, PARTIAL and `from the file you read` sentences; added evals/checks/independent_review/must-pass/{1-none,2-not-blocking} and must-fail/{no-line,file-missing} (findings.md fixtures, fail on ts-rev-form); added evals/calibration/independent_review/{met,unmet}-ts-rev-blockers. Blockers: ts-rev-form/session/commit/step are check-verified and become deterministic with the fixtures (the engine's trust rule), so the audit should clear them; ts-rev-blockers is judge-verified and needs an accepted calibration, which only a model run gives, so the stamp should accept it.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "db401792-76cb-496a-b563-d737a3aa702b"}
