{"t": 928.437, "n": 251, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "The three package test files you named still have one failing assertion, which waits on the stamp. The engine's wider `test_workflow_packages.py` run for `temperspec-tgraph` failed with 20 failures. One of them is the same stamp assertion. I have not fixed the rest, because they are in test files that no row of phase 3 names.\n\n- **`test_phase_coding.py`:** 16 tests fail. I re-ran the file with `-x` and read the first failure. Its stand-in executor, `Stand.run_step` in `test_phase_coding.py` (line 537), has no branch for the new `independent_review` unit, so it raises \"a session of independent_review that the stand-in does not answer\". I take the other 15 to have the same cause, but I read only that traceback.\n- **`test_parallel_reading.py`:** `test_the_records_agree_with_the_setup_survey` also fails. I did not look into it.\n- **Cause:** the new unit is in the run flow (phase 1 or 2 work), and these two files were not updated for it. Either they need a stand-in branch for `independent_review`, as `test_independent_review.py` has, or a row has to name them.\n\nTo resume: phase 3 needs a row, or an earlier phase's rows need extending, so that `test_phase_coding.py` and `test_parallel_reading.py` answer `independent_review`. Then the operator's stamp can go ahead.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran test_independent_review.py, test_spec_budget_and_moved_ids.py, test_temperspec.py (only the stamp-revision test, 23 vs 24, fails; the stamp fixes it) and the engine's test_workflow_packages.py -k temperspec. The last had 20 failures. Of those, 16 are in test_phase_coding.py: its Stand.run_step raises \"a session of independent_review that the stand-in does not answer\" (line 537), and I read only the first traceback. The others are test_parallel_reading.py::test_the_records_agree_with_the_setup_survey (not looked into) and the stamp-revision test. Neither test file is named by a phase-3 row, so I changed neither. They need a stand-in branch for independent_review (a row or an earlier phase's fix) before the code step's suite can pass. Rows 3.7 and 3.8 stay unmarked as asked. Earlier edits this visit: independent_review summary shortened to 56 chars (blueprint.json, diagram/model.json, diagram/workflow.md, workflow/temperspec/__init__.py), judge brief sentences added, evals/checks/independent_review cases and evals/calibration/independent_review/{met,unmet}-ts-rev-blockers added. ts-rev-blockers is judge-verified and needs an accepted calibration, so the stamp should accept it.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "db401792-76cb-496a-b563-d737a3aa702b"}
